tretch our story too far to figure out  how doomsday acquires the gym i mean  sidorak is an extra dimensional demon  right so it's not too far-fetched to  think that we can kind of bend the rules  a little bit and have him travel to the  dc universe  now most of you are probably familiar  with the crimson gem of sidorak as the  object that turned kane marco into the  juggernaut by imbuing him with a  fragment of sidorak's power now as a  result  juggernaut's strength and durability are  greatly enhanced he's equipped with a  force field of mystic energy and most  notably  once he gets moving it's almost  impossible to stop his momentum and in  fact as far as i'm aware of marvel  comics that's only happened once  and so if sidorak had placed the crimson  gem in the dc universe and chose  doomsday as his avatar what would happen  well simply put  doomsday would be one of the most  dangerous forces in the entire dc  universe capable of causing  a nearly unimaginable amount of damage  and so it only makes sense that he would  try and cause that damage where it would  be most likely to draw out his most  hated foe  metropolis and so as our story opens up  we basically see doomsday amped up by  the crimson gem of sidorak  laying waste to the city that superman  calls home and it doesn't take  long for the man of steel to show up and  stop the rampaging doomsday now after  taking a couple of punches however  superman quickly discovers  that doomsday is operating on a level  even beyond anything superman has ever  seen  out of him before and it's not often  that we see superman totally outclassed  in terms of brute strength but because  of the gem's power  he is completely unable to slow down  doomsday's momentum as he runs through  the streets of metropolis leveling  building  after building now superman summons all  of his strength but is absolutely no use  doomsday is simply just  too powerful and is able to defeat  superman with surprising ease  not only because of his enhanced  strength but also because the crimson  gem of sidorak is technically an object  that uses magic energy  and superman is vulnerable to magic  luckily for him before doomsday can  finish him off the rest of the justice  league shows up and engages doomsday now  seeing that superman's badly hurt  batman evacuates him from the scene and  takes him to the justice league  headquarters to recuperate  meanwhile even the combined forces of  wonder woman green lantern flash and  aquaman are having difficulty dealing  with doomsday  realizing they won't be able to defeat  him outright they devise a plan to  remove him from the area  green lantern encases him with a  hard-like construct to keep him from  polarizing her but doomsday almost  immediately breaks free of it this does  however give flash the opportunity to  travel a sufficient distance  and begin running at doomsday now  doomsday continues to run through  multiple city blocks leaving a trail of  rubble in his wake but he's eventually  hit by the flash with the infinite mass  punch  we get an epic moment of two seemingly  unstoppable forces  colliding now although the flash is  clearly capable of moving at a higher  speed than doomsday hitting him head on  proves to be a miscalculation on his  part because hitting doomsday at that  speed  is basically like running into an  immovable brick wall because its  momentum  cannot be stopped while the flash is  able to stall doomsday's movement for a  fraction of a second the collision  temporarily knocks them out cold and so  it's clear by this point that the  justice league is going to have to alter  their strategy to deal with this new  threat and most likely have to call in  reinforcements and here we get a couple  of options one strategy is to try and  bring in the physically strongest  characters they can think of or at least  ones capable of expending the most  energy in the hopes that they'll simply  be able to overwhelm doomsday and so  characters like martian manhunter  supergirl or captain adam are among our  options here on the other hand we have  characters that are adept at using magic  to try and neutralize the gem's power  as for how the justice league would know  that they need someone who can use magic  i think that once superman  recovers enough to the point that he can  talk again he'd basically be able to  sense that there's some other magic at  play  which is one of the reasons he was  defeated so handedly and so as far as  magic users there are plenty of them in  the dc universe we've got john  constantine dr  fate zatanna we really have a ton of  options here now i'm tempted to go with  shazam because he's not only a super  strong character but his powers are  rooted in magic as well but we've never  really seen him using spells which would  probably be required to neutralize the  gem of sidorak  in reality it's more of just a case of  shazam and other's powers being derived  from magic so he's probably not the best  choice we also could just call in  god-like beings like the spectre who  would probably just wipe doomsday from  existence but honestly that doesn't make  for a very interesting story  i think the best option is to have the  justice league recover from this  humiliating defeat  and find a way to defeat doomsday  themselves albeit with a little help  from zatanna and dr fate since they do  need some magical firepower  and they probably wouldn't want to  consult constantine because he's really  just a dick  now in terms of who's going to supply  the brute strength he insists that he'll  be able to be the one  to take doomsday down now as other  members of the justice league try to  talk him out of it due to his weakness  to magic he remains determined to get  back into the battle and defeat his  longtime enemy and so to this conundrum  batman offers a solution and unveils an  armor that he's developed that will not  only shield superman from the jim's  magical energy but greatly augment his  strength as well  now superman of course is hesitant in  dawning the armor as it's not something  that he does regularly but the fact that  he needs it in this situation  shows just how powerful doomsday is when  he's amped up by the crimson gym  and so the justice league converge on  doomsday who's now moved from metropolis  to gotham city  and is wreaking havoc there now at first  doomsday proves difficult for the  justice league to handle even for  superman in his magical resistant armor  and while the armor does alleviate  superman's weaknesses to magic his  strength is still proving insufficient  to stop doomsday's momentum now while it  might seem strange given how strong  superman would be in this situation  we have to remember that even when we  are dealing with kane marco as that  version of the juggernaut a character as  strong as world breaker hulk was  completely unable to stop his momentum  but instead  had to redirect it to end the fight with  him and so while we're dealing with  someone like doomsday who already  possessed strength far beyond kane  marcos he's going to be even more  unstoppable for superman wearing this  armor and so with that in mind the tide  does not turn in the battle  until zatanna and dr fate are able to  neutralize the mystical energies of the  crimson gem and so once doomsday's  connection with the gem is severed  superman is finally able to begin  dealing damage to doomsday and is also  able to endure doomsday's counter  punches thanks to the extra durability  his armor provides  and so once doomsday is sufficiently  weakened the flash would grab him and  then run a good way from the shore now  green lantern would then encase him in a  hard light box that he's unable to free  himself from  immediately due to his weakened state  aquaman would then plunge the box  containing doomsday  into the depths of the sea ridding earth  of the threat that he poses  at least for now dr fate in turn would  take the crimson gem of sidorak and  place it under a magical protection  spell within the tower of fate so that  no one could ever come into contact with  it and become the avatar of sidorak  again  and so yeah that's how i think it would  go down if doomsday got the crimson gem  of cetera  and honestly we could have gone a  different way and we could have chosen  to repeat not only the death of superman  but the entire justice league if we  wanted to go that route but let me know  in the comments and let me know what  stories you guys would like to see me  cover in the future what if episodes and  so with that being said guys we're going  to bring this video to an end  if you are new here to comics explained  make sure you guys hit the sub button to  become part of the rob core if you guys  enjoyed this video make sure you drop a  like  and i will catch you all later peace  [Music]  [Applause]  [Applause]  so  [Music]  you

